  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian Assistance to Returnees in Eastern Chad Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With the arrivals to Chad expected to reach over 1,100,000 people by December 2024, including 240,000 Chadian returnees, tensions related to scarce and/or imbalanced resources including land, water and food continue to increase. The majority of these new arrivals report a lack of food as the main reason for leaving Sudan, demonstrating the development of a complex emergency in Darfur with armed conflict and famine-like conditions which are soon to be exacerbated by the rainy season. With only eleven per cent of needs funded, approximately 65,000 returnees are without access to assistance, with major gaps in the Shelter and Water, Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) Sectors. 
 
To address these gaps, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) is providing vital shelter, WASH and unconditional cash assistance to alleviate the most pressing needs of some 72,240 displaced returnees. This intervention contributes towards the Sudan Emergency Regional Refugee Response Plan for 2024.</narrative>
  </description>
